  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Saturday/...\nNothing much to speak of in the middle of the week as a large \nridge parks itself over the Gulf. A change in pattern is on the \nhorizon, however, as a front makes its way into the panhandle late\nFriday, dropping rain through Saturday. This does not have the \nappearance of a particularly heavy or concerning rain system, but \nit will end the nice weather. Cold air ahead of the front has the \nsnow level pretty low, but the change to southerly flow and slow \narrival of moisture will likely eliminate the confluence of \nfactors necessary for some snow to mix in for low elevation spots \nearly at event onset. Expect a rain event, but as this system gets\nin range for high res models, the rain/snow line will be \nsomething to watch.",
